And I posted a reply/spoiler about how I normally change alignment, but
pressed R instead of F (as I am wont to do) ... distracted chap that I am.
(Sorry for cluttering your mailbox Mike)

Anyway - it went something like this ... (incase anyone else wants to know)

[Spoiler]

First catch your altar - I find Lawful ones are best.

Next - make sure you have 'strayed'.
    To do this when I have just entered the game, I kick my pet to death.
    This works because I am 'nominally aligned' - if you are 'strident'
    you may need to do something more radical to fall from grace.
    Note that strying isn't the same as annoying your God/dess.
Now sacrifice a fresh creature.
    If I have just kicked my pet to death, the body (if any) comes in useful
    here.  Any fresh sacrifice will result in convertion to the new calling.
    Avoid using/wasting unicorns here.
Now get your luck (etc.) back.
    To get into good standing with your new God/dess (you start 'strayed')
    a little more sacrificing is called for.  Do enough of it and you will
    undo the loss of luck that came from the convertion itself.  If you
    have a spare unicorn corpse, now would be a good time to use it.

I didn't think that what you sacrificed had a bearing on the results
(apart from unicorns and humans) - but if anyone can correct me here
(file and line references are best) I'm listening.

